"""Leading with AI (Leadership Edition), Session 12: Leading people through AI: roles, skills, adoption and change.  Practical, NEW in this edition.
Written 12 November 2026.

The leader's question: what happens to my employees, and how do I bring them with me?  Built on Session 11 (the tasks that change) and feeding
Session 13 (the rules around it).  Practical clock (bible): 10 recall, 20 idea with cases, 10 worked example, 5 break, 60 the leader works,
10 decision, 5 close.  No maths: counts, percentages and shillings only.

Cases (research/*.md): BNK-09 Commonwealth Bank of Australia reversal (hook), PPL-09 IMF and PPL-10 ILO exposure, PPL-08 WEF Future of Jobs 2025,
tour tiles BNK-01 Equity, TEL-11 BT, AGR-07 One Acre Fund, MFG-01 Procter & Gamble, HLT-02 Jacaranda Health, PUB-03 SARS; case stories PPL-05 Klarna,
BNK-01 Equity Group, PPL-07 Duolingo; BNK-11 DBS with TEL-11 BT (announced cuts are plans); PPL-12 BCG AI at Work 2025 (frontline stall, shadow AI,
fears, training, guidance); PPL-13 Microsoft skilling pledges (facilitator note only).
Worked example: the Nile Valley Foods customer service officer, redesigned task by task, worked live with the class.  It follows the grey example of
Templates/People and Skills Plan.docx.  The only AI result shown is the Session 11 recorded run (demo_runs/s12_rule_vs_ai.md: Claude, three fresh
sessions, 4 November 2026; AI 9 of 12 exact, 11 of 12 acceptable, one wrong with confidence).  Nile Valley Foods and its staff are fictional.
"""

